questions.q:
'Dividing both terms of a ratio by their HCF always gives the simplest form, but dividing by some other common factor may not.' Justify this statement using the ratio 180 : 240. In your answer:
(a) list three common factors of 180 and 240 other than 1, and divide by each;
(b) find the HCF and reduce the ratio with it;
(c) explain why no further reduction is possible after dividing by the HCF.
